Description: heap-use-after-free in decoder_context::reset() via dangling previous_slice_header
 The issue does not have yet an CVE number assigned.
Origin: https://github.com/strukturag/libde265/commit/07bc500d45f781a7e2915afb7eebc2d6d9a541c9
Bug: https://github.com/strukturag/libde265/security/advisories/GHSA-mm7m-v26f-wf8x

From 07bc500d45f781a7e2915afb7eebc2d6d9a541c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dirk Farin <dirk.farin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 23:55:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix heap-use-after-free in decoder_context::reset()
 (GHSA-mm7m-v26f-wf8x)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

decoder_context::reset() calls dpb.clear() which frees all de265_image objects
and their owned slice_segment_header structs. However, reset() never nulls the
previous_slice_header pointer, leaving a dangling reference into freed memory.

When the next NAL unit after reset() is a dependent slice, slice_segment_header::read()
at slice.cc:435 executes:
  *this = *ctx->previous_slice_header;

This copies from freed 1464-byte struct — heap-use-after-free (CWE-416).

The in-stream case was already guarded by commit 12ba88ec (decctx.cc:556 nulls
previous_slice_header on first slice of new picture). This fix applies the same
invariant to the reset() path: only a slice header still retained by a live image
may remain as previous_slice_header.
---
 libde265/decctx.cc | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/libde265/decctx.cc
+++ b/libde265/decctx.cc
@@ -201,7 +201,6 @@
   set_acceleration_functions(de265_acceleration_AUTO);
 }
 
-
 decoder_context::decoder_context()
 {
   //memset(ctx, 0, sizeof(decoder_context));
@@ -396,6 +395,15 @@
 
   img = NULL;
 
+  // Drop the back-reference to the previous picture's slice header before the
+  // DPB is cleared below. dpb.clear() releases the images, which own and free
+  // their slice_segment_header structs (see de265_image::release()). Leaving
+  // previous_slice_header pointing into that freed storage lets a following
+  // dependent slice read from it (slice.cc: '*this = *ctx->previous_slice_header'),
+  // a heap-use-after-free. This mirrors the in-stream new-picture guard in
+  // read_slice_NAL(): only a slice header still retained by a live image may
+  // remain as previous_slice_header.
+  previous_slice_header = nullptr;
 
   // TODO: remove all pending image_units
 
